{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "8b \u00b7 F9 WALK gait (alt-diagonal) \u2605",
    "description": "[8b \u00b7 F9 WALK gait (alt-diagonal) \u2605] F9 BEST NAV architecture (cognitive PremotorAI + HKE + hit reward + true-compass) BUT with the CPG retuned from trot to an alternating-diagonal walk gait. CPG perceptual_leg_phase_offsets [0, \u03c0, \u03c0/2, 3\u03c0/2] \u2014 swing sequence FL\u2192RL\u2192FR\u2192RR with each leg \u00bc-cycle offset, so the swinging leg's diagonal partner is always in mid-stance (strongest 3-leg support triangle). CruseCoordinator anatomical_anterior wired to match the walk sequence: each leg's \"trigger to swing\" comes from the leg one step before it in the FL\u2192RL\u2192FR\u2192RR cycle. Joseph 2026-06-08: trot's pairwise Cruse messages were destabilizing the body \u2014 one-leg-at-a-time walk should give Cruse a tractable coordination problem. Pair with: picrawler_stand_then_to_target_pb50_2026_06_08 + auto-advance ON.",
    "env_target": "picrawler",
    "phase_tag": "v6.17b + compass + perceptual-cpg trot (Phase 7.5 arm G2)",
    "derived_from_manifest": true,
    "episode_length": 6000,
    "mc_episode_period": 1500,
    "stability_gain": 0.05,
    "stability_y_norm": 0.5,
    "stability_speed": 0.05,
    "reward_shape": "trapezoid",
    "target_height": 0.085,
    "height_penalty_grace": 0.02,
    "height_penalty_scale": 0.03,
    "height_penalty_gain": 0.05,
    "leg_symmetry": "lr_pairs",
    "label": "cruse_v2_baseline"
  },
  "version": 1,
  "runtime": {
    "thread_pool": "per_instance",
    "num_threads": 0
  },
